    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (82.13) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), our two most formidable starts. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a favorable matchup against McGreevy, capitalizing on a significant park and platoon boost to elevate his base projection. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime spot against Singer; the combination of a high-ceiling park environment and a massive +14% platoon edge makes him our most efficient play by total value. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention (74.39), as his matchup against Ober provides a substantial +19% SP skill advantage, keeping him in the elite tier despite a slightly lower raw base.\n\nThe most difficult lineup decision today centered on **Josh Naylor**, who missed the cut at 58.11, falling just short of **Kyle Karros** (59.51) and **Jose Caballero** (56.27). While **Josh Naylor** had a solid profile, **Kyle Karros** secured the 3B spot thanks to a massive +14% park factor, which ultimately outweighed the higher raw efficiency of the bench options. We remain cautious with **Jose Caballero** and **Austin Riley** regarding their respective matchups against Sasaki and Quantrill; although both are started, they carry a -3% penalty for batting in the lower third of the order, which narrowly squeezed them into our active lineup over the more robust projections of our secondary reserves. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility in some of our matchups. **James Wood** (64.81) is a mandatory start, but he faces a unique hurdle today: an elite catcher with a 1.89s pop time, which threatens his stolen base potential despite his 60% hold-SP score. We are also monitoring **Dalton Rushing** (48.93), whose start against Cole is our riskiest deployment; while the platoon advantage keeps him viable, his position in the 8-hole is a significant drag on his overall output. No major weather concerns have been flagged, but we are proceeding with **Gabriel Moreno** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** as reliable core components, both projecting well above the 60-point threshold for strong starts.",
